WEBVTT

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.240
Hello, everybody!

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.650
Hello to all the Memphis Bats fans and everyone who's watching!

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:53.170
Tomorrow we will play our final exhibition game!

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:59.080
The Memphis Bats are located in southern America, in western Tennessee.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.550
Our headquarters are in Memphis, overlooking the Mississippi River.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:06.210
We are a member of the Eastern Division of the West Triple A League.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.600
These six teams are participating in the Eastern Division.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:16.360
There are 140 games in a season. Everyone will be playing in order to enter the playoffs so that they can win the championship.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.980
The Bats are definitely going to win this time!

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.800
We are going to do our best to win the championship, so please come out and cheer for us!

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.290
Go! Go! Bats!

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:25.700
Go! Go! Bats!

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.530
Go! Go! Bats!

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:27.750
Yeah!

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:34.730
This year, both the fans and I are expecting a lot from you guys.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.210
I've also heard there are going to be a lot of journalists and reporters at tomorrow's game.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:43.100
Everyone, make sure you win tomorrow's exhibition game.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.770
Let's do our best and start this season off with energy!

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.980
Who's that!?

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:59.320
Hey, Shigeno, don't sleep!

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.670
So I'll be on the mound tomorrow too? Okay, that's fine with me!

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:17.890
Shigeno sure has stepped it up with his English, hasn't he?

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:18.980
Yeah.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.440
Pitcher, Shigeno!

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:48.330
Congratulations on graduating, everyone!

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:55.460
There is a wonderful blue sky today; a blessing to send you all off.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:01.050
Unfortunately, Shigeno Goro-kun couldn't be here,

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:07.050
but I'm sure he's continuing to do his best under this same sky. 

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:55.730
Yakushiji-kun and Kusano-kun, can we get a picture with all of you together?

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.740
Grandpa! Grandma!

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.620
Congratulations on graduating, Toshiya.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.900
Congratulations.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:13.700
Thank you.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:19.380
We'll be going home ahead of you, so take your time with saying your goodbyes to everyone.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:22.580
Okay, but there's something I want to give you before you go.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:29.220
It was all thanks to you and Grandma that I was able to graduate.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:33.900
You both did your best to help me all this time.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.010
Thank you so much!

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:39.730
I'm going to support you two from now on.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:54.530
What are you saying? We're still able to work, right?

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:56.040
Y-Yes.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:59.620
Don't try to tell old people what to do like you think you know what's best!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:00.530
Hooray! Hooray! Toshiya! Go! Go! Toshiya!

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.680
Hooray! Hooray! Toshiya! Go! Go! Toshiya!

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:02.750
Hooray! Hooray! Toshiya! Go! Go! Toshiya!

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.500
Hooray! Hooray! Toshiya! Go! Go! Toshiya!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.370
Hooray! Hooray! Toshiya! Go! Go! Toshiya!

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:05.290
Hooray! Hooray! Toshiya! Go! Go! Toshiya!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.330
Hooray! Hooray! Toshiya! Go! Go! Toshiya!

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:08.980
Grandpa!

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.010
Grandfather, are you all right?

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.930
Man! That's why I've been telling you not to overdo it.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.450
Hooray! Hooray! Senpai!

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:17.330
Hooray! Hooray! Senpai!

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:18.340
Hooray! Hooray! Senpai!

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:18.890
Hooray! Hooray! Senpai!

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:23.880
Senpai, even though you've already graduated, please stop by and play with us sometime.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.820
Go easy on us when you do.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.470
See you later!

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.720
Shigeno-kun could've at least come back for today, right?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.190
You only get to graduate once, and then it's over.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.030
Aren't you sad, Kaoru?

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.600
N-Not really!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.980
Have you two decided on when you'll see each other again?

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.520
What? Are you serious!?

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.610
You didn't set anything up with him?

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.970
So you don't know when you'll see him again?

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.110
Y-Yeah.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:06.730
Y-Yeah.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.650
He's never been that type of guy.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:17.040
<i>I'll be the first one to get your autograph when you become a pro!</i>

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:27.250
<i>At least let me see your smile one last time.</i>

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:31.480
<i>Do your best, okay?</i>

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:35.550
<i>I won't forgive you if you forget your promise to me about your first autograph, okay?</i>

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.100
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.730
He promised me that he would give me his first autograph.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.670
That's fine though...

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.400
because I still have softball.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.850
I'm going to do my best now!

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:56.360
Senpai, thanks for everything you've done for us.

00:07:57.130 --> 00:08:04.960
We'll work hard to keep the fire you guys ignited burning strong in the Seishuu baseball club.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.010
You know, this isn't how Taiga usually is.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.760
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.630
Hey, new captain, do you have a fever or something?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.510
I wonder if it's going to rain tomorrow?

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.560
Nah, it'll probably snow.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:20.060
No! Then we can't have fun; that wouldn't be good!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:24.080
Okay, okay. Now that we can drop the formalities...

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.150
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.110
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.460
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:34.030
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.580
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.070
My glasses!

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.070
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.490
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:41.910
This is fun...

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.540
Okay, last one, Fuji-senpai!

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.970
I-I'm fine!

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.960
You won't get away, senpai!

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.310
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:52.680
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.430
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.140
Ouch!

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:01.470
I bet you did that on purpose, Taiga!

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:02.970
No, I'd never.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.520
Looks like this is farewell to this earth, huh?

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:22.700
Yeah.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.260
I wonder how he's doing.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:57.460
I'm sure he's doing his very best.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:59.540
Yeah, I think so too.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:00.220
Right?

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.430
Yeah.

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:02.840
Yep!

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:07.030
You're right. Then how about we do our best too?

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:08.310
Sure.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:10.610
Seishuu! Fight!

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:11.270
Seishuu! Fight!

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.380
Yeah!

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:19.320
This is a free fansub.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:19.320
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.200
Now for the moment you've been waiting for, pro baseball fans.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:33.040
Today is finally the opening day for the pennant race!

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:37.240
Look, it's Toshiya! See!?

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:02.970
The ninth batter, Kamihira, is being pinch hit by Sato.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:14.670
I'll be damned if I let a rookie like you hit one of my pitches!

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.630
Strike!

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:27.290
Toshiya!

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:27.290
It went over!

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:31.680
Sato hits a grand slam walk-off homerun in his first at-bat!

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.530
Strike!

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.290
Strike! Batter Out!

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:02.130
The game's over! The Oceans' new rookie, Mayumura, claims his first victory as a pro with a complete game!

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.980
<i>I can finally play baseball again.</i>

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.150
Hey, new guy! Get in line!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.360
Yes, sir!

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:30.330
Nice to meet you!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.340
I'm the captain, Shimizu Taiga.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.560
"Our goal is to defeat Kaido..."

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:38.250
is a totally reckless statement that you'll never hear from me.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:42.170
So, for now, let's just make sure we get to Koshien.

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:46.780
Isn't that the same thing as telling everyone to defeat Kaido?

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.890
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.730
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.350
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.850
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:20.790
I envy Miyazaki. He was accepted into the university of his choice.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:26.210
Uchiyama was also able to get into the school that he wanted to go to.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:30.330
And here we are, living a rounin's life as buddies...

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.560
I can't hear anything! Be quiet!

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:53.450
All right!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.160
Okay, last one!

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.410
Okay, go for it!

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:06.470
Thanks a lot!

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.470
So, what do you think of the ballpark in spring?

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:07.230
The atmosphere's so different from an exhibition game that you're stunned into silence, right?

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.070
Let's do this!

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.400
That's more like it!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:13.060
Go! Go! Bats!

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:13.570
Go! Go! Bats!

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:13.950
Go! Go! Bats!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:14.320
Go! Go! Bats!

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:16.280
Yay!

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:25.460
Good! A double play!

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:28.040
Safe!

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.000
Throw it back home!

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:45.450
You've got to be kidding. He scored.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:48.730
We need a new pitcher. Put Frank in.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:51.230
Strike out!

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:53.240
Strike out!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:57.200
All right! Now for our rally!

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.130
Yeah!

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.250
Yay!

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:14.550
Attention please, now pitching, number 56:

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:18.510
Goro Shigeno!

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:40.280
Let's do this!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.920
Wow! He struck them both out with three pitches!

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:52.000
There's only one left! Shigeno-kun!

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.550
Strike out!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:57.930
All right!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:06.250
We did it! We managed to win our first game of the season!

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:09.300
Congratulations!

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.150
You too, Coach!

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:17.450
Quit screwing around, Matt!

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:20.990
What's going on!?

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.850
Is this Sergeant Sanders' usual lecture?

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.010
Y-You've really done it now, you bearded gorilla!

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.510
Y-You've really done it now, you bearded gorilla!

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.040
Beat him up, Matt!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:34.670
You bastard!

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.710
What gives you the right to come back here early...

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:40.970
and drink beer without a single care in the world, when you, our ace pitcher, got knocked out in the second inning!?

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.130
You say it's not a problem since we managed to rally,

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:47.390
but is it really appropriate behavior for this season's ace to be drinking like this!?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.870
Cut it out already, you lecturing old fart!

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.900
I didn't make the only error in the game!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:19:00.850
If Roy and Kelloge had turned the double play like they were supposed to, I wouldn't have been replaced!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.060
Shut up!

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.920
What I'm trying to tell you is that it's your fault for pitching poorly in the first place,

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.080
and not accepting any responsibility for it on top of it all!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.830
An ace should be good enough to support everyone!

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.510
Hey, Matt,

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.460
that wasn't my fault!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.500
It was Roy's crappy timing!

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:19.760
What did you say!?

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:23.990
Come on! Quit blaming things on other people!

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.560
Shut up!

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:31.730
Q-Quit it, you old geezers! Someone could get hurt!

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.940
Cut it out!

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.810
Are you all right?

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.890
Does it look like I'm all right!?

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:58.050
Really, why did you start a fight when we won today?

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:01.960
I'm sorry, Miss.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:06.300
Save your energy for the game instead!

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:14.230
Even if we have all this strength on our team, we won't be able to win unless we work together!

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:21.930
It'll be impossible to win this year as well, Miss.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:28.740
At least with Shigeno we have a really good closer.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:33.150
We improved our fielding in training camp.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:37.120
And our offense, as usual, is strong.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:42.560
However, we can't win with just that.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:49.930
Putting aside teamwork, the main problem is that no one aims for the championship in the Minors.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:55.270
It's normal for the owner of a team,
like you, to aim for the championship,

00:20:55.820 --> 00:21:02.500
but most of the players on the Bats are looking for a shot to rise up to the Majors.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:06.460
"We can win in the Minor League as many times as we want,

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:09.430
but if we can't rise to the Majors, then there's no point."

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:12.460
That's what all the Triple A players are really shooting for.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:16.510
Isn't that what you're after too, Shigeno?

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:19.670
Y-Yeah, pretty much.

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:23.840
Isn't it the same way for you?

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.410
I'm already 34.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:32.760
I threw away my dream of rising to the Majors a long time ago.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:39.390
In the Minors, these are my final hours.

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:46.880
If that's the case, then I'd like to taste victory just once with the Bats, as thanks for taking care of me for seven years.

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:54.950
Even so, it's impossible to convince the youngsters.

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:00.330
It's not impossible!

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:03.170
I understand now!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:06.670
No wonder I thought I'd teamed up with a bunch of half-hearted guys.

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:12.010
Because they don't go for the win, they just sit around and rot.

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:16.150
I'm going to help you, old man!

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:19.730
Let's make sure the Bats win the championship this year!

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:21.900
Shigeno!

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:24.500
W-Well...

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:28.110
Even if we both want to-

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:29.870
Don't give up just yet!

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:32.050
We can do it!

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:34.120
We can change the way the Bats think!

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:11.800
All right!

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:13.560
"Let's do our best to win the championship."

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:19.560
That's what I'd like to say, but everyone's making stupid mistakes!

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:22.280
Don't they want to rise up to the Majors!?

00:24:22.280 --> 00:24:24.050
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:25.350
Let's Aim For It.

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:28.020
Run to the stage of your dreams!
